 Everything under Chapters keeps working as normal.
 
+### Your invitation
+
+When the platform sets a book up for you, your GitHub account is invited to it.
+After you sign in, the invitation is at the top of the list of books: press it
+to accept, and the book is chosen. Nothing needs doing on GitHub's website.
+
 ### Which book
 
 Everything under **Waiting for you** belongs to **one book at a time**. The band
diff --git a/docs/word-to-markdown.md b/docs/word-to-markdown.md
index d2d9236..9221fed 100644
--- a/docs/word-to-markdown.md
+++ b/docs/word-to-markdown.md
@@ -373,22 +373,26 @@ Once the checklist passes:
    yours should too. If a stray blank line or a duplicate title has been left at
    the very top, delete it.
 
-2. **Add the chapter to the front page.** Open **`index.md`** and add a bullet
-   under **Contents**, copying the shape of the one already there:
-
-       - **[[chapter-05|Chapter 5 — Photosynthesis]]**
-         One sentence saying what the chapter covers.
-
-3. **Get the chapter and its pictures into `drafts`.** The book is its
-   repository on GitHub, and the chapter reaches readers only from there.
-
-   > **To confirm:** whether the app commits a converted chapter and its
-   > `assets/<chapter-name>/` pictures to `drafts` itself (the platform's plan
-   > calls this "Send to drafts", BOOK-ONE-TO-QUARTZ §8 step 1), and what the
-   > button says. Until that is confirmed, a chapter the app saved to a folder on
-   > your Mac is not in the book: ask the technical contact to put it on
-   > `drafts`, or follow what `docs/what-this-book-runs-on.md` records for your
-   > copy of the book.
+2. **Send it to drafts.** On the screen showing the converted chapter, press
+   **Send to drafts**. The chapter and its pictures go into the book's drafts
+   area as one change, made by you. You need to be signed in (the book list
+   shows your book); if you aren't, the screen says so before you convert.
+
+   A **new** chapter also gets one line on the book's front page, under
+   **Contents**, in the same change, and you are shown the line before you send:
+
+       - **[[chapters/Chapter 5|Chapter 5: Photosynthesis]]**
+
+   Nothing else on the front page changes. You can add a sentence under the line
+   later, in the browser. Bringing the same Word file in again replaces the
+   chapter and leaves the front page alone.
+
+3. **Keep Word as your copy.** To change the chapter later, edit the Word file
+   and bring it in again under the same name. The app shows how many lines
+   differ and who last changed the chapter, and asks you to confirm the
+   replacement. A change someone else made on the website since then (an
+   accepted reader suggestion, say) is replaced too, so make the same change in
+   your Word file first.
 
 4. **Check it on the drafts preview, then go live.** Once the chapter is on
    `drafts` it appears on the drafts preview within a few minutes. Read it there,
